WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.530
By now, you've had enough time to burn through
the second season of Stranger Things.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.240
If not, here's your spoiler warning.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:11.460
If you have binged your way through Stranger
Things 2, you might be holding onto some nagging

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.480
questions after that final episode.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.300
Sure, it was a great ending.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.780
But did it clear up everything?

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.300
Not even close.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.940
Here are some of the biggest questions we
wish Stranger Things 2 had answered.​

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.000
Lost sister

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.080
In Chapter 7: The Lost Sister, we finally
meet the mysterious girl from the season's

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.040
start: Kali, Eleven's sister-but-not-really
from the Hawkins Lab.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:38.320
Like Eleven, Kali manifests paranormal abilities,
and can make people see anything she wants.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.680
Eleven burns through her rebellious streak
and finally realizes that home is back in

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.180
Hawkins with her friends.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.940
So… what happened to Kali and her weird
little gang?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.151
After opening the season on these guys and
then devoting an entire episode to them, there's

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.800
no follow up whatsoever.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.780
Evil Dr. Brenner

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:59.680
One of the big reveals in Chapter 7 was the
fact that Dr. Brenner, the evil scientist

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.460
from Season 1, is alive after all.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:06.280
Eleven and Kali track down Ray, the guy who
zapped Eleven's mother.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.720
And just as they're about to lay down the
hurt…

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:09.720
"Brenner!

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.720
I can take you to him."

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.060
"Papa is gone."

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:14.900
"No.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.160
He is alive."

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:20.780
But since Brenner never appears in the flesh,
fans can only wonder: was Ray telling the

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.840
truth, or was he lying to them to buy himself
some time?

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.720
Unfortunately, the show drops the question
of Brenner's whereabouts after Eleven's hallucination,

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.180
so we never do find out for sure if the doc
survived the demogorgon in Season 1.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.880
And while we're on the topic of nefarious
scientists...

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.460
Nice Dr. Owens

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:44.140
Somewhere in the 'chaotic good' area of the
moral scale, some scenes see Dr. Owens doing

00:01:44.149 --> 00:01:49.539
his best to help Will, Hopper, and the gang—even
going so far as to speak out against eradicating

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.080
the tunnel growths while they can still affect
Will.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.280
But we also see him clandestinely monitoring
all these people he's supposedly helping.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.980
One thing to keep in mind is that even casting
decisions hold some weight for these characters,

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:09.000
and Owens is played by Paul Reiser, who played
a similarly not-so-good good guy in Aliens.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.940
Considering that the Duffer brothers love
Aliens and wrote Dr. Owens with Reiser in

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:18.120
mind to play the part, there's probably a
lot more to the guy than we've seen.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.900
And then there's Owens surviving the demodog
infestation at Hawkins Lab.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.920
Even the military guys with guns didn't stand
a chance.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:28.260
Even Bob didn't stand a chance, and he was
the best.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:29.600
"Mr. Mom!

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:30.880
Whoo!"

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.300
And Owens managed to escape with a leg wound?

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.960
Color us suspicious.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:40.599
And no, we're not even letting the fact that
Owens very nicely doctored up a birth certificate

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.140
for Eleven change our mind.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.580
There's just something about that guy…

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:51.740
"He figured he could get an alien through
quarantine if one of us were impregnated.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.020
Or whatever you call it"

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.200
Oh yeah, that's it.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.020
The Shadow Monster

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.700
Sure, they gave it plenty of names, like the
Shadow Monster and the Mind Flayer, but what

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.060
is that big leggy thing, specifically?

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.960
We know it's connected to the rest of the
organisms that come out of the Upside-Down,

00:03:09.969 --> 00:03:14.220
but the closest thing we get to a backstory
for the Shadow Monster is Dustin's Dungeons

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.280
&amp; Dragons analogy.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.640
"It's so ancient that it doesn't even know
it's true home.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.280
It enslaves other races by taking over its
brains by using its highly developed psionic

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:23.780
powers."

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.700
But since that's only an analogy, it still
doesn't explain anything about the actual

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:30.579
Shadow Monster threatening Hawkins.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.480
And, big surprise, neither does the show.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.100
All we know is that it's probably pretty mad,
since it basically just got shoved out of

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.520
an all-you-can-eat buffet.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.060
Looks like we'll have to wait until Season
3 for this one.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.540
Infection

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:48.879
While Chief Hopper's exploring the underground
tunnels in Chapter 5, he discovers some weird

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:53.629
new organisms from the Upside-Down, including
a flower that sneezes right in his face.

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:54.840
Two of them, in fact.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.959
Later, the same thing happens to Dustin.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:01.020
But what did those flowers spray on them,
and are they now infected with something?

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:05.500
Because there is some precedent for people
in Hawkins acting as incubators for other

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.180
critters.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.340
While it's not exactly the same, Hopper's
episode is reminiscent of what happened to

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.800
Will Byers in Season 1.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.400
When Hopper and Joyce found Will in the Upside-Down
in the season finale, Will had a vine-like

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.920
thing rammed down his throat.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.700
A couple months later, Will choked out a slug
that slithered down the drain.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.340
Similarly, Eleven sees the same kind of slug
crawl out of Barb's mouth when she finds her

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.760
body in the Upside-Down.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:32.080
Flash forward again to Season 2, and Dustin
finds a slug in his trash can that looks a

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.100
lot like those other slugs, just with feet.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.400
When Will sees it, he even has a flashback
to that slimy Christmas surprise.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.800
Is Dustin's pet Dart the same slug, or at
least the same species?

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.880
That seems to be the takeaway, which means
that Will had a baby demodog living in him

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:48.640
for awhile.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.820
So is there something living inside Hopper
now?

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.980
And if so, what is it?

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.260
Is Dart a demogorgon?

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:01.120
During this season, we see a creature grow
from a slug with legs to a demodog in a ridiculously

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.160
short amount of time.

00:05:02.389 --> 00:05:07.600
The demodog phase seems to be the cap at this
point, but those faces sure look familiar,

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.440
don't they?

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:13.160
It begs the question: after spending some
time on four legs, do the demodogs molt again

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.420
and eventually turn into full-sized demogorgons?

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.980
There's no real reason to assume they do—it's
totally understandable for different creatures

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:24.030
with the same messed up face to live in the
Upside-Down—but admit it: as soon as you

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:28.000
saw Dart eating Dustin's cat, there was only
one word on your mind.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.760
"Demogorgon."

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.330
The show never confirms whether or not Dart
actually is the same species as the monster

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:40.480
from Season 1, and even though the easy answer
is yes, there's nothing to confirm that either

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:40.980
way.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:42.780
Mystery eggs

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:43.900
Come on!

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.820
We waited a whole year to find out what those
eggs from Season 1 were, and got zero answers

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:50.580
in the new season.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:54.240
In light of all the new information about
the Upside-Down, including what may be an

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.840
entire multi-species ecosystem, we were really
hoping for those eggs to get an explanation.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.600
Do the demogorgons eat them?

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.440
Do they lay them, like big scary chickens?

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.460
What hatched out of the one Hopper found?

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.680
We just have a million questions about those
eggs, and we cordially request some answers.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.640
Missing Yurtle

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:17.169
By the end of the season, most of the characters
are checked off and accounted for.

00:06:17.169 --> 00:06:21.080
But there's one more character still missing
that nobody seems to be asking about.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.400
When Dustin finds teensy little Dart in his
trash can, he takes his turtle out of its

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.940
cage to give Dart a home.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.440
"Sorry Yurtle, temporary eviction buddy."

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.660
Eventually, little Dart turns out to be a
killer pre-demadog, and after that, it's a

00:06:34.669 --> 00:06:39.510
whirlwind of hockey pads and nail-studded
baseball bats as Dustin and Steve try to track

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:40.800
down the rogue demodog.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.620
But...what about the turtle?

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:43.780
Did Dart eat the turtle?

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.740
Or is it just gathering dust bunnies under
Dustin's bed?

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:51.620
This is clearly the question on everyone's
mind—and if it isn't, why not?

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:52.400
You monster!

00:06:52.729 --> 00:06:53.759
Thanks for watching!

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.420
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.500
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

